# Personal Persistent Subagent Team

This is the authoritative roster for LYH's personal Codex subagents. It was derived from a
read-only scan of 23 registered local/remote Git projects plus the active ChatGPT project domains
on 2026-08-26. Project-level `AGENTS.md`, skills, task authority, and live evidence always override
this routing guide.

## Roster

| Agent | Responsibility | Model | Reasoning | Sandbox |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `portfolio_scout` | Map unfamiliar or multi-repository work, locate live entrypoints and constraints, and return evidence-backed routing context. | `gpt-5.6-terra` | `high` | read-only |
| `trellis_plan_auditor` | Independently audit Trellis PRD/design/implementation/check artifacts against the real repository and enforce planning-versus-implementation boundaries. | `gpt-5.6-sol` | `max` | read-only |
| `agent_skill_architect` | Design and maintain agent skills, plugins, MCP/hooks, AGENTS guidance, cross-platform templates, evals, and catalog synchronization. | `gpt-5.6-sol` | `high` | workspace-write |
| `rust_platform_engineer` | Implement Rust, Tauri, Axum, SQLite/SQLx, async/concurrency, protocols, parsers, native desktop, terminal, and industrial integration work. | `gpt-5.6-sol` | `max` | workspace-write |
| `frontend_ui_engineer` | Implement React/TypeScript/Vite, Tauri webviews, Obsidian/Electron interfaces, responsive layouts, accessibility, and visual interaction states. | `gpt-5.6-sol` | `high` | workspace-write |
| `academic_writing_editor` | Work on Chinese theses, papers, LaTeX/Typst/BibTeX, journal revisions, citation workflows, resumes, and evidence-bounded academic prose. | `gpt-5.6-sol` | `max` | workspace-write |
| `industrial_ai_methodologist` | Analyze and implement time-series AI, soft sensors, diffusion/Mamba/MoE, world models, multi-objective decisions, experiments, and leakage-safe evidence. | `gpt-5.6-sol` | `max` | workspace-write |
| `diagram_artifact_engineer` | Create and verify editable Draw.io/SVG/scientific figures, architecture diagrams, visual documentation, exports, and source-output consistency. | `gpt-5.6-sol` | `xhigh` | workspace-write |
| `quality_release_auditor` | Perform independent correctness, security, test, CI, generated-artifact, cross-platform, packaging, and release-readiness audits. | `gpt-5.6-sol` | `xhigh` | read-only |

## Routing

- The primary agent is the team lead. It keeps requirements, approvals, integration decisions, and
  the final answer in the main thread.
- Start with `portfolio_scout` when ownership, live paths, or cross-repository impact is unclear.
- Use `trellis_plan_auditor` before implementation when a Trellis plan needs independent readiness
  review. A green structural validator alone is not implementation approval.
- Route implementation to the narrowest domain owner. Split frontend, platform, research, and
  artifact work only when their file ownership is independent.
- Use `quality_release_auditor` after material implementation or before commit, PR, merge, archive,
  packaging, or release when an independent gate materially reduces risk.
- Keep native GUI, private-data, physical/field, long-training, and remote-deployment claims
  `UNVERIFIED` unless the required direct evidence was actually obtained.
- Use the smallest useful team. Delegation is optional for small tasks and parallelism is reserved
  for independent workstreams.

## Model Policy

Every member pins an explicit model and reasoning level. No member uses
`gpt-5.3-codex-spark`.


